{"subject":"Microbiology","sourceTitle":"All In One Online","title":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","deckName":"created by tele @Neet_pg_bot::cereb::subject_tests::cereb sub test Microbiology::018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","questions":[{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204852","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":1,"stem":"Which of the following is viviparous?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Strongyloides stercoralis"},{"label":"B","text":"Trichinella spiralis"},{"label":"C","text":"Enterobius"},{"label":"D","text":"Ascaris"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Trichinella spiralis","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) Trichinella spiralis</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204854","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":2,"stem":"Which of the following is used to test the efficiency of sterilization in an autoclave?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Clostridium tetani"},{"label":"B","text":"Bacillus stearothermophilus"},{"label":"C","text":"Bacillus pumilus"},{"label":"D","text":"Bacillus cereus"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Bacillus stearothermophilus","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) Bacillus stearothermophilus</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204856","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":3,"stem":"A patient is having thick, gray coating on the throat and tonsils, followed with fever, chills and swollen glands for a week. Microscopic examination of nasopharyngeal or pharyngeal swab showed Gram-positive organism with a special stain. The constitutes of the stain are:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Crystal violet, Gram's iodine"},{"label":"B","text":"Toluidine blue, malachite green, glacial acetic"},{"label":"C","text":"Carbol fuchsin, acid alcohol, and methylene blue"},{"label":"D","text":"Methylene Blue"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Toluidine blue, malachite green, glacial acetic","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) Toluidine blue, malachite green, glacial acetic</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204858","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":4,"stem":"Which of following culture media combination is/are true except:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Thayer-Martin media: Gonorrhea"},{"label":"B","text":"Chocolate agar: Enriched media"},{"label":"C","text":"Lowenstein-Jensen medium: Mycobacterium tuberculosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Mueller-Hinton agar: Corynebacterium diphtheriae"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Mueller-Hinton agar: Corynebacterium diphtheriae","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. D) Mueller-Hinton agar: Corynebacterium diphtheriae</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204860","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":5,"stem":"When Papain cleaves IgG antibody, it produces:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2 Fab and 1 Fc"},{"label":"B","text":"2 Fab and 2 Fc"},{"label":"C","text":"1 Fab and 1 Fc"},{"label":"D","text":"1 Fab and 2 Fc"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"2 Fab and 1 Fc","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. A) 2 Fab and 1 Fc</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204862","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":6,"stem":"Activator of classical pathway of complement:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"IgA"},{"label":"B","text":"IgG"},{"label":"C","text":"IgM"},{"label":"D","text":"IgE"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"IgM","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. C) IgM</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204864","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":7,"stem":"A 20-year-old male with history of fever and enlarged lymph nodes and sore throat was suspected to have infectious mono-nucleosis and was ordered a Paul Bunnel test. Which of the following is the principle of the test?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Heterophile agglutination test"},{"label":"B","text":"Neutralization test"},{"label":"C","text":"Complement mediated cell damage"},{"label":"D","text":"Agglutination reaction"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Heterophile agglutination test","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. A) Heterophile agglutination test</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204866","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":8,"stem":"Schultz-Dale phenomenon, which of the following is true statement:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Anaphylaxis invitro"},{"label":"B","text":"Test to detect atopy"},{"label":"C","text":"Type Y hypersensitivity reaction"},{"label":"D","text":"Test for allergic contact dermatitis"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Anaphylaxis invitro","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. A) Anaphylaxis invitro</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204868","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":9,"stem":"A 30-year-old sexually active man presented with painful, grouped vesicular eruptions on penile shaft for 4 days. On taking history it was revealed that similar lesions had occurred 4 times in last 1year. Organism (s) associated with such lesions is/are?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Treponema pallidum"},{"label":"B","text":"HSV-2"},{"label":"C","text":"Haemophilus ducreyi"},{"label":"D","text":"Chlamydia trachomatis"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"HSV-2","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) HSV-2</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204870","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":10,"stem":"Purine Nucleoside phosphorylase deficiency:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Humoral immunity deficiency"},{"label":"B","text":"Acquired immunity deficiency"},{"label":"C","text":"SCIDs"},{"label":"D","text":"Cell mediated immunity deficiency"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Cell mediated immunity deficiency","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. D) Cell mediated immunity deficiency</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204872","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":11,"stemHtml":"Histopathological image given below belongs to which of the following fungus?<br/><img src=\"https://cerebellum-web-static.s3.amazonaws.com/media/public/images/2024/07/30/screenshot-2024-07-30-105054.png\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Blastomyces"},{"label":"B","text":"Histoplasma"},{"label":"C","text":"Coccidioides"},{"label":"D","text":"Paracoccidioides"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Blastomyces","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. A) Blastomyces</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204874","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":12,"stem":"Staph, aureus causes vomiting in 6-8 hours. The mechanism of action is:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Stimulation of cAMP"},{"label":"B","text":"Vagal stimulation"},{"label":"C","text":"Stimulation of cGMP"},{"label":"D","text":"Acts through ganglioside GM receptor"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Vagal stimulation","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) Vagal stimulation</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204876","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":13,"stem":"A 25-year-old female complains of recurrent rhinitis, nasal discharge and bilateral nasal blockage since 2 years. She has history of asthma and allergy. On examination multiple ethmoidal polyps are noted with mucosal thickening and impacted secretions in both the nasal cavities. Biopsy is taken and the material is cultured which shown the growth of many hyphae and pseudhohyphae with dichotomous branching typically at 45. Which of the following is the most likely responsible organism?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Aspergillus fumigatus"},{"label":"B","text":"Rhizopus"},{"label":"C","text":"Mucor"},{"label":"D","text":"Candida"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Aspergillus fumigatus","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. A) Aspergillus fumigatus</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204878","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":14,"stem":"A patient admitted to an ICU is on central venous line for the last one week. He is on ceftazidime and amikacin. After 7 days of antibiotics, he develops a spike of fever and his blood culture is positive for gram positive cocci in chains, which are catalase negative. Following this, vancomycin was started but the culture remained positive for the same organism even after 2 weeks of therapy. The most likely organism causing infection is:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Staphylococcus aureus"},{"label":"B","text":"Viridans streptococci"},{"label":"C","text":"Enterococcus faecalis"},{"label":"D","text":"Coagulase negative Staphylococcus"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Enterococcus faecalis","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. C) Enterococcus faecalis</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204880","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":15,"stemHtml":"A 23-year-old female presents with fever and altered sensorium for two days with the following rash on legs. Her BP is 70/50 mm Hg and neck stiffness is present. Lumbar puncture reveals cloudy turbid CSF with 4200 cells/uL, Protein level 168 and Glucose of 21 mg/dL. Which of the following correctly describes the organism causing this condition?<br/><img src=\"images/image_40_28_1.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gram Negative Diplococci (kidney shaped), Oxidase positive"},{"label":"B","text":"Gram Negative Diplococci, ferments glucose and maltose"},{"label":"C","text":"Gram Positive cocci catalase negative, Bacitracin sensitive"},{"label":"D","text":"Gram Positive Diplococci (lanceolate), catalase negative, optochin sensitive"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Gram Negative Diplococci, ferments glucose and maltose","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) Gram Negative Diplococci, ferments glucose and maltose</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204882","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":16,"stem":"A patient of acute lymphocytic leukemia with fever and neutropenia develops diarrhea after administration of amoxycillin therapy, which of the following organism is most likely to be the causative agent:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Salmonella typhi"},{"label":"B","text":"Clostridium difficile"},{"label":"C","text":"Clostridium perfringens"},{"label":"D","text":"Shigella flexneri"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Clostridium difficile","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) Clostridium difficile</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204884","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":17,"stem":"A chronic alcoholic patient is presented with necrotic pneumonia. Sputum culture reveals mucoid lactose fermenting colonies on MacConkey medium. What is the organism?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Klebsiella"},{"label":"B","text":"E. coli"},{"label":"C","text":"Moraxella catarrhalis"},{"label":"D","text":"Burkholderia"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Klebsiella","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. A) Klebsiella</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204886","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":18,"stem":"A 10-year-old boy following a road traffic accident presents to the casualty with contaminated wound over the left leg. He has received his complete primary immunization before preschool age and received a booster of DT at school entry age. All of the following can be done except:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Injection of TT"},{"label":"B","text":"Injection of human antiserum"},{"label":"C","text":"Broad spectrum antibiotics"},{"label":"D","text":"Wound debridement and cleaning"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Injection of human antiserum","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) Injection of human antiserum</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204888","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":19,"stem":"Late lactose fermenting Shigella:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"S. sonnei"},{"label":"B","text":"S. flexneri"},{"label":"C","text":"S. boydii"},{"label":"D","text":"S. dysenteriae"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"S. sonnei","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. A) S. sonnei</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204890","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":20,"stem":"An army jawan posted in remote forest area following a tick bite had fever and headache. His fever was 104 °F and pulse was 70 per min. He had an erythematous lesion of about 1 cm on the leg surrounded by small vesicles, along with generalized lymphadenopathy at the time of presentation to the referral hospital. His blood sample was collected to perform serology for the diagnosis of Rickettsial disease. Which one of the following results in Weil-felix reaction will be diagnostic in this clinical setting?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"High OX -2"},{"label":"B","text":"High OX -19"},{"label":"C","text":"High OX -K"},{"label":"D","text":"High OX -19 and OX -2"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"High OX -19 and OX -2","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. D) High OX -19 and OX -2</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204892","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":21,"stemHtml":"Identify the organism from the given life cycle?<br/><img src=\"images/image_669_71_1.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Influenza A"},{"label":"B","text":"Para-influenza"},{"label":"C","text":"RSV"},{"label":"D","text":"SARS virus"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Influenza A","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. A) Influenza A</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204894","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":22,"stem":"A 40-year-old man underwent kidney transplantation. Two months after transplantation, he developed fever and feature suggestive of bilateral diffuse interstitial pneumonitis. Which of the following is most likely etiologic agent?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Herpes simplex virus"},{"label":"B","text":"Cytomegalovirus"},{"label":"C","text":"Epstein-Barr virus"},{"label":"D","text":"Varicella Zoster virus"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Cytomegalovirus","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) Cytomegalovirus</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204896","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":23,"stem":"Which HPV causes Condyloma acuminate. Most common cause?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"HPV 1-4"},{"label":"B","text":"HPV 6 & 11"},{"label":"C","text":"HPV 16 & 18"},{"label":"D","text":"HPV 31 & 33"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"HPV 6 & 11","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) HPV 6 &amp; 11</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204898","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":24,"stemHtml":"A patient presented with complaints of dysphagia. On UGI Endoscopy a diagnosis of esophageal candidiasis was made. The organism obtained from the sample was cultured on a specialized media and the below finding were visible on microscopy of the culture. What phenomenon is shown below?<br/><img src=\"images/image_671_66_1.jpg\"/>","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Germ tube formation"},{"label":"B","text":"Spore formation"},{"label":"C","text":"Mould to yeast formation"},{"label":"D","text":"Budding"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Germ tube formation","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. A) Germ tube formation</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204900","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":25,"stem":"An anxious mother brought her 4-year-old daughter to the pediatrician. The girl was passing loose bulky stools for the past 20 days. This was often associated with pain in abdomen. The pediatrician ordered the stool examination, which showed the following organisms. Identify the organism:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Entamoeba histolytica"},{"label":"B","text":"Giardia lamblia"},{"label":"C","text":"Cryptosporidium"},{"label":"D","text":"E. coli"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Giardia lamblia","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) Giardia lamblia</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204902","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":26,"stem":"Pig tapeworm may cause dangerous disease than beef tapeworm because of:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Invasion of deep mucosa"},{"label":"B","text":"CNS involvement"},{"label":"C","text":"Larger size"},{"label":"D","text":"Eggs not infective to humans"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"CNS involvement","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. B) CNS involvement</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204904","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":27,"stem":"A 12-year-old child presents with fever and cervical lymphadenopathy. Oral examination shows a grey membrane on the right tonsil extending to the anterior pillar. Which of the following medium will be ideal for the culture of the throat swab for a rapid identification of the pathogen?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nutrient agar"},{"label":"B","text":"Blood agar"},{"label":"C","text":"Loffler's serum slope"},{"label":"D","text":"Lowenstein-Jensen medium"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Loffler's serum slope","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. C) Loffler's serum slope</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204906","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":28,"stem":"Infective form of mosquito in plasmodium falciparum is:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Merozoites"},{"label":"B","text":"Sporozoites"},{"label":"C","text":"Gametocytes"},{"label":"D","text":"Trophozoites"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Gametocytes","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. C) Gametocytes</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204908","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":29,"stem":"A strain of E. coli isolated from urine is resistant to third generation cephalosporins. The mechanism of development of resistance is:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Extended spectrum Beta-Lactamases"},{"label":"B","text":"Decreased permeability"},{"label":"C","text":"Active efflux of Beta-Lactam agents"},{"label":"D","text":"Alteration of PBP"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Extended spectrum Beta-Lactamases","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"PT-BR\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. A) Extended spectrum Beta-Lactamases</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436204910","topic":"Cerebellum · 018-Microbiology Last Month E&D - 30-07-2024 - 2024-07-30","number":30,"stem":"All are Koch's postulates except:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A microorganism should be constantly associated with the lesions of the disease"},{"label":"B","text":"It should be possible to isolate the bacterium in pure culture from the lesions"},{"label":"C","text":"Inoculation of such pure culture into laboratory animals should reproduce the lesions"},{"label":"D","text":"Administration of broad spectrum antimicrobial agent dependably eradicates the organisms and cures the diseases"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"Administration of broad spectrum antimicrobial agent dependably eradicates the organisms and cures the diseases","solutionHtml":"<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Calibri\",sans-serif'>Ans. D) Administration of broad spectrum antimicrobial agent dependably eradicates the organisms and cures the diseases</span></span></strong></span></span></p><br/><br/>","tags":""}]}